<title>HONG KONG: S.China Holdings 1996 net down 45.72 pct.</title>
<headline>S.China Holdings 1996 net down 45.72 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   15.1	 vs 27.9</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.5	  vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	21.36 gain vs 134.78 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    57.52	vs 105.96</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,765.71   vs 1,987.75</p>
<p>    Company name		 South China Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 4-6</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   June 23</p>
<p>NOTE - South China Holdings is an investment holding and property investment company.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$17.47 million on disposal/dilution of interest in an associated company/a subsidiary and gain of HK$3.89 million on restructuring of a subsidiary.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 11 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 4.5 cents) vs 12 cents (including interim dividend and special bonus).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
